 {(filename1 filename2)}←CompareCommits(space folder args);hash1;hash2;exe;name;buff
⍝ Desc: Compares two different commits
⍝ Parse: 2s -project= -use= -files
⍝ Project: 0
 (hash1 hash2)←{0≡⍵:'' ⋄ ⍵}¨args.(_1 _2)
 'Argument is invalid'Assert(,'.')≢hash2
 buff←folder ##.CompareCommits hash1 hash2
 (filename1 filename2 hash1 hash2)←4↑buff,'' ''    ⍝ Because old versions of CompareCommits did not return the hashes
 (hash1 hash2)←{⍵↑⍨¨8⌊≢¨⍵}hash1 hash2              ⍝ Short version suffices
 :If 0<+/⎕NEXISTS filename1 filename2
     :If args.files
         exe←''                                    ⍝ The user asked for the filenames, so don't bother the comparison utility
     :Else
         (exe name)←##.U.EstablishComparisonTool''args.Switch'use'
     :EndIf
     :If 0=≢exe
         ⎕←filename1 filename2
     :Else
         {}name ##.U.CompareTwoFiles(filename1 filename2)(folder∘##.U.GetCommitCaption¨hash1 hash2)
         ⎕NDELETE filename1 filename2
         (filename1 filename2)←⊂''
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
